**Bug found and fixed:**

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to access the second element of the split array instead of `parts[0]` to access the first element. This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass successfully.
